Z||000002||RossT||02-28-2001||03:51 AM||||I care!! Did you splice the factory wire harness to attach to the pioneers, or did you make or buy a speaker wire adapter to plug into the factory wire harness?<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 02-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe4x4||02-28-2001||06:20 AM||||Was it hard..I`m thinking of putting in new speakers in the front and rear.<BR>What did you use, price and where you get them.<BR>Do you have pics?<BR>was it hard in the front?<P>------------------<BR>Fiero got fire<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exp.gif">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||02-28-2001||09:21 AM||||When I installed mine, I cut off the factory plug and soldered the wires right to the speaker.  <P>The hardest part of the install is getting to the screws closet to the windshield.  A stubby or right-angle screwdriver makes it alot easier.  Other than that it's pretty easy.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Homicidal||02-28-2001||12:22 PM||||I'll throw some pics up when it's a little less rainy, so hold on, I will get some!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The original speakers had some form of wire adapter already on there, I could tell it was a stock adapter though.  So I spliced the wire into the new wire adapters that the speakers came with, simple and easy.<P>The speakers are Pioneer and I got them for $68 at Employeee Cost at Circuit City (my job).  Normally $99 for them.<P>120W Max<BR>35 Nominal<BR>4 Ohm<P>Nice set!||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||02-28-2001||12:49 PM||||when i installed my 4x10s, i just ran new speaker wire from the unit to the speakers. not that hard to do. so i didn't have to cut anything.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bruce||02-28-2001||05:26 PM||||Maybe it's just me, but I think the stock speakers sound better than the Kenwood's I bought. I figured that since I was replacing the speaker grill fabric. I'ld pop in some new 4 x 10's. I'm thinking the Pioneers may be a better selection.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||02-28-2001||05:40 PM||||bruce, something must be seriously wrong if your stock speakers sound better than the kenwoods, or any aftermarket speakers. you maybe have something hooked up wrong. do you have an aftermarket head unit, or the stock one? because, if you don't have enough watts to power a speaker, it isn't gonna sound good. (yeah i know, the speakers probably don't need a lot of power anyway)||||reg||1
