Z||000013||Eric||03-01-2001||11:56 PM||||I like it!  I've got those exact speakers ridin' in my car.  No need for a sub, just the 4x10s will suffice.  I always turn the bass selector up and you can hear and see my car going, "THUMP THUMPY THUMP".  Ahh, I guess I'm just getting a little carried away.  <P>Don't have  any solutions for your dash problem, but try painting your speaker fabric.  Flat black cheapie spray worked for me.  Just make sure to rinse them in soap and water first.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Homicidal||03-02-2001||12:04 AM||||*shudder* A stereo without a sub?<P>No way!  I sub isn't for only bass buffs, it adds a new dimension to ALL music.  I was astounded at all the low bass lines I was missing in many songs before I had a sub.<P>Especially for rock, those bass guitars can really add a "heavy" feel to rock.<P>The best bad I have heard to use bass with rock for the hardest sound is Sevendust, awesome.||||reg||1
